  "method": "Copied fixture world; fixed camera; unpaused terrain warmup, then paused rendering. 8-second settle, 30-second capture, 3-second callback flush. Metal drawable presentedTime measures displayed presentation rate; CPU includes game and wineserver. 100% CPU is one logical core. Native presentation trace is identical across variants.",
  "limitations": [
    "One scene on one machine, not an average across gameplay/worlds. Clouds/entities and exact warmup timing vary between launches.",
    "A1/B1 are exploratory, with less controlled focus/warmup. A2 before warmup is explicitly excluded: missing terrain caused a false 100 FPS control.",
    "A2-warm and A3-warm bracket B2-warm. Controls vary 67.67\u201377.56 FPS; B2 = 99.95 FPS. No single guaranteed percentage is justified.",
    "Native requested minimum presentation interval is 10 ms; candidate approaches this 100 FPS ceiling.",
    "This improves throughput, not total CPU use or RAM. CPU per displayed frame changes modestly; total CPU rises with extra frames.",
    "Original-vs-candidate confirmation uses identical diagnostic DXMT with frontend profiling off. These values are not mixed with clean-DXMT comparisons.",
    "Stack sampling through Rosetta could not establish exact allocator critical-path mechanism.",
    "Per-thread attribution before A2 used unstable TLS addresses and is excluded. Later stable kernel IDs provide near complete coverage; process CPU remains primary."
